@meeting introBriefing
// Day 1, Monday 07:50, the Works bay: Calder's Monday briefing, Torres and two Works crew on shift (cast 'works:2':
// the script's tech1 and tech2). The Works writer. Calder hands you to Torres in two sentences. One choice, no wrong answer.
title: Monday briefing
from: Chief Ines Calder
gist: The Monday briefing: Calder put you with Torres for the day. One job, end to end, with your own hands.
== lines
calder: Ten to eight. Good. Everyone's here.   [nod]
calder: Board's at twelve. Two scrubbers, a lamp on Deck 4, the dish pit. A usual Monday.
calder > you: {me}. Arrived last night. Works, from today.
tech1 > you: Morning, new hand.   [gesture]
tech2 > you: Welcome to Works. Tea's at half ten. That's the important bit.
calder: Torres. One job, end to end. Board to turn-in. Their hands, not yours.
torres-zeke: Their hands. Got it, Chief.
? choice
* Ready when you are.   rel:torres-zeke+1 flavour:cheer
  torres-zeke: That's the spirit. Right, onward.   [laugh]
* What if I get something wrong?   rel:calder+1 flavour:listen
  calder: Then you say so, and we fix it. That's the job.
* (Nod)
  calder: Good. Quiet's fine.
calder: Right. Board's there. Back to it.
